# The detector and its test are where the signatures are DEFINED, so they match
# themselves. Nothing else may carry a vendor mark, and that is the point: this
# file names two paths, not a pattern, so an allowlist entry cannot quietly grow
# to cover a page that really does ship someone else's branding.
#
# Left unlisted, `vendormark .` failed on this repo for every build — it read its
# own CONTENT_SIG literal and reported the tool as a violation. A gate that
# cannot pass over a correct tree teaches people to ignore it, and this one had
# been red on main long enough for that to start.
bin/vendormark
bin/vendormark_test.sh
